Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `b`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/ownership/view_in_returned_record_field_outlives_its_owner.jet:13:13
    |
 12 |     Keep{v: b.head()}
    |             ^^^^^^
 Why: `b` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
